## The six research vectors are allocated by operation

| Experiment | Primary product work | Required neighbouring work / discriminator |
|---|---|---|
| E1 Seam retention | S1 Actuation retains exclusion and conditions of judgment | S2 makes the relevant source/alternative operative; S0 supplies attribution. Retention must change an available revision, not just a displayed trace. |
| E2 Gauge disclosure | S1 Actuation exposes reference/evaluator | S0 identifies who can revise the commission; S3 returns labour and adverse evidence. A changed explanation and a changed criterion remain distinct. |
| E3 Lens refraction | S5 QL/MEF supplies the declared lens operation; S1 receives the changed judgment | S2 resolves the scoped resources. Compare actual question, evidence and judgment, keeping the complete pair and version fixed. |
| E4 Topological continuity | S5 supplies formal continuity comparisons; S1 carries the judgment landscape | S0 retains attributable maps. Mapper and sheaf proposals remain distinct constructions with their own observations and limitations. |
| E5 QL recursion | S5 nested whole/part differentiation | S1 interprets and acts; S2 places the selected frame. Removing a named relation must expose the exact operative difference being tested. |
| E6 Deferential return | S1 revises an act’s conditions; S3 integrates the resulting changed form | S0 can receive a revised source/commission; S4 returns material consequence; S5 retains the containing relation. A next act must be governed by the returned difference. |

